WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.543 --> 00:00:03.917
- [Kelly Clarkson]
Hello, you look so good!

00:00:05.913 --> 00:00:08.010
They don't do that for everyone.

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:08.897
- [Faith Hill] Yeah, they do.

00:00:08.897 --> 00:00:10.938
- No, they don't! You look so great!

00:00:10.938 --> 00:00:11.771
- You look amazing!

00:00:11.771 --> 00:00:12.610
- You look fantastic in this!

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:13.443
- I've missed you!

00:00:13.443 --> 00:00:15.540
- I know, I'm never anywhere but here.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.220
- I mean, you are working
your tail off, girl!

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:18.960
- I know, I'm taking the summer off.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:19.793
I'm very excited.

00:00:19.793 --> 00:00:22.590
It's my first summer
off since I was like 16.

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:23.423
- Really?

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:25.190
- Yeah. And you know, when things happen

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:26.147
that's when people start going,

00:00:26.147 --> 00:00:27.240
"Hey, but I have this.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:28.140
Hey, but there's this."

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:30.450
And you're like "No".

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:32.250
But speaking of girls, I have to say

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.210
this is one of my best moments of my life.

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:36.040
I've had a few times that
I've randomly run into her

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.600
and pretended it was totally normal.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.217
I was with Reba and they were like,

00:00:39.217 --> 00:00:40.050
"We're going to this dinner!"

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:41.250
and all of a sudden, you're there.

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:43.030
And I was like, "Yeah,
it's totally normal."

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:45.690
I'm like ♪It matters to me♪

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:46.860
I totally wanted to see-

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:48.560
Do you remember this night though?

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:50.503
Do you remember?

00:00:50.503 --> 00:00:52.000
- [Faith] Yes! Yes!

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.367
- [Kelly] I went to go see Shania.

00:00:54.367 --> 00:00:55.200
You did too.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.033
I was with Reba

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:58.562
and I was pretending

00:00:58.562 --> 00:01:01.510
I was Meryl Streep right there.

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:03.930
I was so chill about it.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.610
But legit, I was so excited.

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:06.527
- No, same.

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:08.787
- [Kelly] My friends
afterwards, we were just like,

00:01:08.787 --> 00:01:11.490
"Do you remember how I
pretended that was normal?"

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:13.680
I was very excited about that
night but I was wondering,

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:15.230
cause we just were talking
about girls nights out,

00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:16.370
do you do that with your daughters?

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:18.650
Do you ever say, "Tim you're
not allowed" and you just go?

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:19.790
- [Faith] It just happened.

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:21.540
- [Kelly] It just
happened? What'd y'all do?

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:24.690
- Well, he was not allowed
because he was actually working.

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:26.880
- [Kelly] Oh, that's a
good time to do it though.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:27.747
- It is, yeah.

00:01:27.747 --> 00:01:28.580
- Cause then you don't feel as bad.

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:30.617
You're like, "Well you're
working, it's your fault."

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.290
- That's one way to look at it, I guess.

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:36.890
Gracie, our oldest, we
have three daughters,

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:39.753
Gracie just turned 25 last week.

00:01:41.432 --> 00:01:45.140
This week, we went on a girls' trip

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:47.110
and had the best time,

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:51.060
the four of us together
and Gracie's best friend.

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:53.360
Girl, I'm all about the dancing.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:54.570
- Oh, I love dancing.

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:55.403
- [Faith] I cannot dance at all

00:01:55.403 --> 00:01:57.350
and I'll be the first to admit it.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.920
I know I can't dance, but I do not care.

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:01.170
I don't care.

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:03.970
- It should be whatever
it should be though.

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:07.150
It feels good just to move your body.

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:08.607
- It should be whatever it should be.

00:02:08.607 --> 00:02:10.990
That's when people go, "Mm-hm, 'kay."

00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:12.377
- [Kelly] No, you know what they say?

00:02:12.377 --> 00:02:13.850
Look, I just went to a concert

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:14.870
Lemme tell ya, this lady in the front-

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:16.770
I was like, One, what are you on, ma'am,

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:19.740
and two, she was living her best life

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:21.360
and it was beautiful to watch.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:24.669
Like she was just so into it,
moving, and it feels good.

00:02:24.669 --> 00:02:27.117
- [Kelly] So now is a
look at her show "1883".

00:02:27.117 --> 00:02:29.600
You can see it on Paramount Plus.

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:33.310
This show, "1883" it's your
first major acting role?

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:35.481
'Cause I know that you
were in "Stepford Wives",

00:02:35.481 --> 00:02:36.314
- Yes!

00:02:36.314 --> 00:02:37.640
- and you've been in some things.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:39.130
I love that one.

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:42.860
So was it something that
you've always wanted to do

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:44.100
and you dipped your toes in a little bit

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.810
but then you decided to just jump in?

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:48.060
- Yes. I started singing in church,

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:49.750
but the first thing that I did,

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:52.430
when I was in lower school,
middle school, high school,

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:54.410
were plays. I was on stage all the time.

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:56.310
Then my career took off,

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:57.980
no time, had babies.

00:02:57.980 --> 00:02:58.900
Kept on having babies.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:01.350
It felt like I was having
babies all the time,

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:03.280
and I had done a couple of things.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.960
I did "Stepford Wives" with an amazing cast.

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:08.420
Amazing cast.

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:10.100
It wasn't the best experience.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:14.290
So I said I will never, ever, ever, ever

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:18.070
do anything like that, a
movie, because it took so long.

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:19.920
The waiting for me,
you have to understand-

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:20.850
- Hurry up and wait

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:24.620
- I cannot, I have to be busy doing stuff.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:28.213
Anyway, then I did an independent
thing called "Dixieland".

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:30.603
You know,

00:03:30.603 --> 00:03:33.530
I've read a lot of scripts
over the years and-

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:34.610
- [Kelly] Nothing ever really hit ya?

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:37.800
- Nothing hit me or the
timing wasn't right,

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:42.800
and for the script to have been
so incredibly well written,

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:45.380
I honestly had never
read anything like it.

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:46.887
We're talking about "1883".

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:54.010
So we just made the decision to do it.

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:56.611
Tim and I have been
married 26 years this year.

00:03:56.611 --> 00:03:59.637
- Congratulations. That can be hard.

00:03:59.637 --> 00:04:00.470
- Really?

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:01.928
- Not all of us make it.

00:04:01.928 --> 00:04:02.837
- It's okay girl.

00:04:02.837 --> 00:04:03.740
- That's amazing!

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:05.770
Were you excited about doing it together?

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:06.603
- [Faith] Gosh, yes.

00:04:06.603 --> 00:04:07.580
- Or were you a little intimidated by it?

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.610
- [Faith] Well, I'm intimidated by him

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:13.620
because he's an amazing
actor, first of all.

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:15.360
All of the actors on the show,

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:19.573
everyone was so top of the game,

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:22.853
behind the camera, in front of the camera,

00:04:24.607 --> 00:04:26.300
but I did have to say,

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:28.480
I did have the rule, for me, personally,

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:30.590
because we've been together for so long,

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:32.683
and we are together all the time-

00:04:33.517 --> 00:04:34.503
It's glorious.

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:41.636
- We love it. We love
it. All the togetherness.

00:04:41.636 --> 00:04:43.053
- It is the best!

00:04:44.003 --> 00:04:44.973
It's so good.

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:47.700
- 24/7

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:48.683
- 25/7

00:04:48.683 --> 00:04:51.540
- It is kind of cool
though, the different role.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:52.800
Is it cool to play someone back then?

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:56.060
'Cause you shot in Texas, my own state,

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:57.850
also, I live in Montana as well

00:04:57.850 --> 00:04:58.990
and you shot in Montana as well.

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:00.550
So, wait, that's really
hot or really cold.

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:01.600
Which one was harder?

00:05:02.665 --> 00:05:04.320
- Okay. I'm from Mississippi,

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:05.840
so the humidity, the heat I could-

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:06.700
- [Kelly] You're kind of used to that.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:09.380
- I could deal with it. Texas though was-

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:10.230
- It's God's hairdryer.

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:12.023
- [Faith] Different. That's good!

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:13.820
But the cold,

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:17.930
the wind combined with the cold in Montana

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:20.620
was almost too much to bear.

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:21.865
It is off the chart.

00:05:21.865 --> 00:05:25.080
- [Kelly] If you're not
dressed properly, it slaps you.

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:28.800
- [Faith] It really pierces
your entire everything.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:30.087
But my rule with Tim, I said,

00:05:30.087 --> 00:05:31.700
"Look, if we're gonna do this together,

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:34.870
we cannot run lines together, ever.

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:37.420
We cannot talk about the scene

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:40.580
that we're filming tomorrow, ever,"

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:43.559
because it's like-

00:05:43.559 --> 00:05:44.392
- You wanted it to feel fresh

00:05:44.392 --> 00:05:46.240
and you want it to be
something else separate?

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:48.440
- [Faith] Well, that was, in my opinion,

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:53.440
the only way for me to bring-

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:57.620
to make it feel real and authentic

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:00.530
and it had to be when
the cameras were rolling,

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:02.020
we're on set, roll.

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:05.430
That was the first time I
met James, was on that set

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:08.263
and we were working together
when we were filming.

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:12.277
I know him so well so
otherwise I'd have been like,

00:06:12.277 --> 00:06:14.590
"Hmm maybe you shouldn't do that."

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:15.866
You know what I'm saying?

00:06:15.866 --> 00:06:16.917
- [Kelly] And then you start judging it.

00:06:16.917 --> 00:06:19.090
- "Don't do your face like
that when you say that word."

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:21.206
And him to me, the same.

00:06:21.206 --> 00:06:23.650
I'm, again, being funny.

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:26.068
- Again, being funny. She loves him.

00:06:26.068 --> 00:06:28.215
- So much! I do, I really do.

00:06:28.215 --> 00:06:29.923
- [Kelly] She loves him! I know, I know.

